// Title: Forest Blizzard APT - JavaScript Constrained File Creation
// Sigma ID: ec7c4e9b-9bc9-47c7-a32f-b53b598da642
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2024-04-23 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685.001
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects the creation of JavaScript files inside of the DriverStore directory. Forest Blizzard
//   used this to exploit the CVE-2022-38028 vulnerability in Windows Print Spooler service by
//   modifying a JavaScript constraints file and executing it with SYSTEM-level permissions.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2024/04/22/analyzing-forest-blizzards-custom-post-compromise-tool-for-exploiting-cve-2022-38028-to-obtain-credentials/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules-emerging-threats/2024/TA/Forest-Blizzard/file_event_win_apt_forest_blizzard_constrained_js.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\System32\\DriverStore\\FileRepository\\" and FolderPath endswith "\\.js"
